.TH MULTILOG 1 "2026-07-23" "rgbdns 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
multilog \- collect and rotate service logs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B multilog
.RB [ t ]
.RB [ s\fIsize\fR ]
.RB [ n\fIcount\fR ]
.I directory
.RI [ directory ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copies standard input to a
.I current
file in every destination directory. Files rotate before a write would exceed
99999 bytes, and 10 old files are retained by default.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B t
Prefix each input line with a TAI64N timestamp.
.TP
.BI s size
Set the rotation size in bytes (1 through 2^40).
.TP
.BI n count
Retain this many rotated files (1 through 10000).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tai64n (1),
.BR tai64nlocal (1)
